# tests/mpx3-boreutils' run list (px12, M-PX3). kmain_boreutils runs it
# from the initramfs as /etc/pax-run; tools/linux-run runs it chrooted on
# Linux; the two outputs and exit statuses are compared byte for byte.
# One command a line, words separated by single spaces, the first the
# program's path. The milestone's five first (echo, cat of a file, ls of
# a directory, wc, head; px15: boreutils' own ls, where px12 had
# busybox-static's), then
# the rest of what px12 implemented: a seeking reader (tail, pread64 and
# lseek), getcwd (pwd), several files, a relative path, end-of-file on
# standard input, clock_nanosleep (sleep), two programs at once (a
# sleeper woken after ls ran must find its own FS base: commands
# separated by " & " run together on PAX, one after another on Linux),
# "." and ".." (ls -a), and three errnos as each utility words them
# (ENOENT, EISDIR, ENOTDIR). Then bu18's twelve ls lines (boreutils
# notes/bu18/pax-mpx3-with-ls.patch): -l refused by name, columns at a
# given width, -R, -d, -S, a missing operand.
/bin/echo hello from boreutils
/bin/cat /etc/motd
/bin/ls /bin /etc
/bin/wc /etc/words
/bin/head -n 3 /etc/words
/bin/tail -n 2 /etc/words
/bin/pwd
/bin/wc /etc/motd /etc/words
/bin/cat etc/words
/bin/head -n 1 /etc/motd
/bin/cat
/bin/sleep 0.2
/bin/sleep 0.3 & /bin/ls /etc
/bin/ls -a /etc
/bin/cat /etc/nothing
/bin/cat /bin
/bin/head -n 2 /etc/motd/x
/bin/ls /etc
/bin/ls -l /etc
/bin/ls -a /bin
/bin/ls -F /etc /bin
/bin/ls -R /etc
/bin/ls -a -C -w 40 /bin
/bin/ls -x -w 30 /bin
/bin/ls -m /bin
/bin/ls -d /etc /bin/ls /etc/motd
/bin/ls -S -r /etc
/bin/ls /nothing /etc
/bin/ls -d /
